65bp.\n- Norvane Utilities priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. Its 2027 capex is up 12%, so it looks able to fund its plan.\n- Pellham Power, the largest buyer of grid equipment, plans 2027 capex up 18%. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\".\n- The documents don't say whether Pellham is held back by its balance sheet or by market conditions. I infer leverage or rating limits, but that is my inference.\n\n**Equity: mostly no.**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short.\n- Two utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3 2026.\n- Small or discounted raises may still get done, but large ones like Pellham's can't.\n\n**Net:** Debt can fund the plans in aggregate, at higher cost. Expect Norvane's 2027 spending to come in broadly on plan and Pellham's to come in below plan.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- Norvane is the only confirmed debt deal.\n- I have no data on other Caldrian utilities.\n- I have no figure for the size of the funding gap.\n\nDetails are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":2097,"type":"result","duration_ms":32695,"uuid":"6ecdd4e2-b1e7-4300-99b3-3c7e3cfd059c","ttft_stream_ms":1297,"time_to_request_ms":93,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":38,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":67,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":183,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":109,"process_rss_mib_result":196,"process_anon_mib_result":115